WEBVTT

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.594
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.410
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:21.238
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.238 --> 00:00:28.885
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.893 --> 00:00:33.164
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.050
But, with you...

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.160
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.720
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:47.440
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.820
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.841 --> 00:00:53.421
Just to survive!

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.360
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.362 --> 00:00:57.225
Take this moment...

00:00:57.225 --> 00:01:00.820
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.059
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:04.870
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.580
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.710
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.420
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.126
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.126 --> 00:01:18.298
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.292 --> 00:01:20.133
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:24.042
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:34.210
You're including Q Class in this case?

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.044
Yes.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.213
But, Dan-Sensei...

00:01:38.088 --> 00:01:43.552
...normal classes have at least a year of training
before they are assigned to a real case.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.724
I realize they are exceptional, but to dispatch
them on such a difficult case...

00:01:48.849 --> 00:01:50.976
...without warning is a little...

00:01:52.102 --> 00:01:54.021
I made a promise to them.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.734
To teach them everything I know
about being a detective.

00:01:59.276 --> 00:02:00.027
But...

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:03.781
My time is running short.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:06.408
Dan-Sensei...

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:15.417
This isn't good!

00:02:15.417 --> 00:02:16.961
I'm late, I'm late!

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.004
Watch out!

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:20.756
Yo, Kyuu!

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.218
Why are you in such a rush, Kyuu?

00:02:25.719 --> 00:02:27.638
It's already 3:30!

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:29.807
Class is about to begin!

00:02:30.224 --> 00:02:31.559
It's only 3:00, isn't it?

00:02:31.892 --> 00:02:32.476
Eh?

00:02:32.643 --> 00:02:33.477
That can't be...

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:37.606
I-It got me.

00:02:38.274 --> 00:02:39.942
Such a simple, psychological trick...

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:44.405
To stop it right when class is supposed to begin!

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.157
That's not really a trick.

00:02:47.408 --> 00:02:49.743
Hey, something's happening!

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.412
What's wrong?

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:55.082
We don't have time to discuss it here!

00:02:55.207 --> 00:02:55.833
Eh?

00:02:58.419 --> 00:03:00.087
Class seating examination?

00:03:01.672 --> 00:03:06.343
The test allows students from other classes
to switch with the members of Q class.

00:03:06.969 --> 00:03:07.803
When is it?

00:03:08.137 --> 00:03:10.264
There's no date scheduled.

00:03:10.598 --> 00:03:11.765
Is this for real?

00:03:12.057 --> 00:03:13.517
Don't act so surprised.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.768
Yukihira-san!

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.522
Our friends from Q class, it's been a while.

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:22.151
Shishido-san, Gouda-sen and Shiamine-sen...

00:03:22.818 --> 00:03:23.485
Likewise!

00:03:24.486 --> 00:03:28.198
There are several class seating
examinations every year.

00:03:28.991 --> 00:03:33.495
We made our way up into A
Class through these exams.

00:03:34.038 --> 00:03:37.625
But now, the new Q Class is
ranked higher than A Class.

00:03:38.542 --> 00:03:43.839
Normally, we should be able
to switch into Q Class.

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:46.425
Dan-Sensei responded with this...

00:03:47.301 --> 00:03:53.557
The four top ranked in A Class are superior
to Q Class in analytical ability.

00:03:53.724 --> 00:03:55.893
Um, what about me?

00:03:56.185 --> 00:03:59.480
We'll prove that fact in the next exam.

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:08.989
Well, after the test make sure you don't let
the second raters in B Class overtake you.

00:04:10.324 --> 00:04:11.116
C'mon, guys.

00:04:13.369 --> 00:04:16.205
If you can't even make D
Class, you're out of here.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.374
Wait, guys!

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.584
Hold on, dammit!

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:21.835
Sounds good to me!

00:04:22.044 --> 00:04:23.796
Let's settle it now!

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.382
I can't wait for the exam!

00:04:26.924 --> 00:04:28.592
Wait, Kinta!

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:32.346
Kinta, don't go flying of the hook on your own.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.140
Interesting.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.605
I also thought that waiting for
the exam is a bit annoying.

00:04:42.523 --> 00:04:45.317
Interesting conversation you're having.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:47.695
Dan-Sensei!
Dan-Sensei!

00:04:48.195 --> 00:04:50.948
Then, shall we hold the exam today?

00:04:51.448 --> 00:04:53.033
Eh? Today?
Eh? Today?

00:04:53.617 --> 00:04:55.119
Really, Sensei?

00:04:55.411 --> 00:04:56.036
Yes.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:02.167
I will present a problem for the five students
in both A Class and Q Class to solve.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:05.838
Call it a "deductive battle".

00:05:06.463 --> 00:05:07.673
A deductive battle?

00:05:08.465 --> 00:05:10.676
Furthermore, if A Class wins...

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:15.597
...I will, on my authority, switch the
members of Q Class with A Class.

00:05:16.098 --> 00:05:19.685
S-Switch Q Class with A Class?

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.603
C-Crap.

00:05:21.895 --> 00:05:23.647
Kinta, you moron!

00:05:24.231 --> 00:05:26.900
A deductive battle, sounds fun!

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.236
Then, it's decided.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:36.035
I've done some more in-depth
research on those four...

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.787
...and I've found some additional information.

00:05:39.288 --> 00:05:41.123
I'll start with Gouda Kyousuke-san.

00:05:41.582 --> 00:05:43.459
He calls himself the Puzzle King...

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:50.007
...but he's really a mathematical genius. At 17 he
was ranked in the World Mathematics Olympics.

00:05:50.674 --> 00:05:53.510
What, he's not really the Puzzle King?

00:05:54.178 --> 00:05:54.928
How disappointing.

00:05:55.179 --> 00:05:56.138
Quiet, you!

00:05:56.388 --> 00:06:00.476
Shiramine Hayato-san was raised by
his father, a famous world magician.

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:04.229
Since his debut in Las Vegas at the age of
eight, has remained the prince of magic.

00:06:04.772 --> 00:06:08.984
Wow, he really is good with magic!

00:06:09.777 --> 00:06:17.117
Shishido-san studied at Harvard and received
his doctorate in Criminal Psychology at 20.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:19.328
His doctorate...

00:06:19.661 --> 00:06:21.830
Yeah, but Yukihara-san...

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:23.707
You're wrong.

00:06:23.999 --> 00:06:27.628
Yukihara-san is the author of several
best selling mystery novels.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.803
This is the problem I have for you.

00:06:37.012 --> 00:06:39.848
This case occurs in a small
village in the mountains.

00:06:40.516 --> 00:06:44.311
A college student, who visited
the village with his friends...

00:06:44.728 --> 00:06:46.605
...was reported missing.

00:06:47.397 --> 00:06:50.275
They say he vanished without a trace.

00:06:50.692 --> 00:06:51.610
Vanished without a trace?

00:06:52.486 --> 00:06:53.904
So, that's the village?

00:06:54.696 --> 00:06:57.908
This footage was taken by a friend who was...

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.287
...with the missing student
in Kamikakushi village.

00:07:03.831 --> 00:07:06.041
This was taken before the planting season.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:07.543
Planting season?

00:07:07.835 --> 00:07:09.002
How do you know?

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:12.256
There's a thin layer of water covering the field...

00:07:12.714 --> 00:07:14.133
...but nothing has been planted on it.

00:07:16.552 --> 00:07:18.137
Now, there are footprints.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.849
One set of continuous footprints.

00:07:23.183 --> 00:07:24.351
I wonder where they lead?

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:29.648
Eh?

00:07:31.733 --> 00:07:32.651
The footprints...

00:07:33.569 --> 00:07:35.404
They disappear in the middle of the field?

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:39.825
It's like... they vanished mid-step!

00:07:40.367 --> 00:07:41.910
The friend that took this footage...

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:46.206
...found these strange footprints
with a few of his acquaintances.

00:07:47.082 --> 00:07:50.752
As such, there has been no tampering
with this footage.

00:07:52.087 --> 00:07:58.552
These footprints begin at the missing
student's room window.

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:02.598
It's as though he was enticed to
leave though the window...

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.934
...and vanished into thin air
midway through the field.

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:08.061
Into thin air...

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.772
When they found the footprints...

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:14.193
...there wasn't enough evidence to
label this a missing person case...

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.237
...so the police never investigated.

00:08:19.031 --> 00:08:22.868
However, it wasn't long before villagers
began circulating a rumor.

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:30.125
"Yet another has been spirited away
while searching for the treasure."

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.922
The Case of the Disappearance into Thin Air.

00:08:36.173 --> 00:08:38.175
This is getting pretty exciting!

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:46.975
It's a diorama.

00:08:48.101 --> 00:08:48.685
<i>Yes.</i>

00:08:49.311 --> 00:08:52.814
It's a diorama of the scene replicated
at a ratio of 72:1.

00:08:53.523 --> 00:08:56.318
Amazing, they even have a tractor!

00:08:56.860 --> 00:09:00.447
Just as when the footprints where found,
the water has been drained.

00:09:01.657 --> 00:09:08.038
Even the gates that allow the water to
flow in and out have been recreated.

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:13.669
I'd like you all to solve the Case of the
Disappearance into Thin Air using this.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:15.504
Dan-Sensci...

00:09:15.963 --> 00:09:18.215
When did they discover the footprints?

00:09:19.132 --> 00:09:21.385
At 7:00 am, before breakfast.

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:25.764
And when was the student last seen?

00:09:26.765 --> 00:09:28.183
At 10:00 pm the night before...

00:09:28.809 --> 00:09:31.853
...at the giant bath in the hotel.

00:09:32.896 --> 00:09:33.605
I <i>see.</i>

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:37.401
If we think of this as a murder...

00:09:38.151 --> 00:09:40.696
...and estimate he was killed within
an hour of leaving the baths.

00:09:40.904 --> 00:09:43.782
If this was before the planting season...

00:09:45.158 --> 00:09:49.079
...sunrise should be around 5:50 am.

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:52.541
If this was done in the dark, then...

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:56.586
...the perpetrator would only have
five to six hours to work with.

00:09:57.212 --> 00:10:00.299
Hey, there's still no evidence
that this is a murder!

00:10:00.799 --> 00:10:02.634
We did use the word "if", didn't we?

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:06.471
And, since the student is still missing...

00:10:07.055 --> 00:10:08.974
...it's possible that he's already dead.

00:10:09.975 --> 00:10:13.312
Then whose footprints are those in the field?

00:10:13.937 --> 00:10:15.314
Obviously the perpetrators.

00:10:16.106 --> 00:10:19.860
His intention was to make it
look like a vanishing act...

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:24.698
...so using some sort of trick, he
left those footprints behind.

00:10:25.866 --> 00:10:26.575
That's right.

00:10:27.534 --> 00:10:29.578
From what Dan-Sensei has said...

00:10:29.953 --> 00:10:35.792
...and considering the village's
name which means to vanish...

00:10:36.918 --> 00:10:42.382
...everyone would assume the victim
had been spirited away.

00:10:43.258 --> 00:10:46.303
I'm sure that was the perpetrators goal.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:49.723
Hmm, that could be right.

00:10:49.723 --> 00:10:53.018
C'mon, this is no time to be impressed!

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.604
But, that was a brilliant deduction!

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.106
No wonder they are in A Class!

00:10:59.566 --> 00:11:00.317
Geez!

00:11:01.151 --> 00:11:03.236
Hey, how does this sound?

00:11:03.945 --> 00:11:08.742
The perpetrator made the footprints by walking
backwards in the victim's shoes?

00:11:10.535 --> 00:11:12.329
What makes you think it was backwards?

00:11:12.704 --> 00:11:13.288
Huh?

00:11:13.413 --> 00:11:15.540
Well, it just came to me...

00:11:16.041 --> 00:11:17.125
...like a sixth sense!

00:11:17.667 --> 00:11:18.418
Sixth sense?

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:21.421
His idea is a good start.

00:11:22.005 --> 00:11:23.131
Oh, you think so?

00:11:23.507 --> 00:11:27.636
It's easier to get to the middle without
making any footprints...

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:31.348
...than to vanish after walking to the middle.

00:11:31.973 --> 00:11:36.520
So, walking backwards does make sense.

00:11:37.729 --> 00:11:38.438
But...

00:11:39.231 --> 00:11:40.899
...from the diorama...

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:45.904
...there's nothing near the field that you could
use to attach wires and reach the middle...

00:11:46.196 --> 00:11:48.740
...such as a tree or a building.

00:11:49.908 --> 00:11:50.784
Dan-Sensei...

00:11:51.368 --> 00:11:52.285
I've got it!

00:11:53.078 --> 00:11:55.247
No way, you solved it?

00:11:55.872 --> 00:11:56.748
Please explain.

00:11:57.374 --> 00:12:01.711
In this case, there is only one
possible explanation.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:06.174
The key points are this tractor and planter.

00:12:06.383 --> 00:12:10.470
That is, since a building or
tree cannot be moved...

00:12:11.471 --> 00:12:16.852
...the tractor and planter can be
moved to wherever you see fit.

00:12:17.936 --> 00:12:21.648
First, the planter is moved to the center...

00:12:22.232 --> 00:12:25.986
...and a wire capable of supporting a person's
weight is strung across the field.

00:12:26.653 --> 00:12:32.409
Then, the perpetrator carefully inches
across the wire like a ranger...

00:12:33.493 --> 00:12:35.954
...to create the scene that we see.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:40.375
That's the answer!

00:12:40.876 --> 00:12:41.710
I see.

00:12:45.464 --> 00:12:46.423
you're wrong,
How's that?

00:12:46.756 --> 00:12:47.340
Eh?

00:12:47.632 --> 00:12:49.426
Umm, why?

00:12:50.218 --> 00:12:55.557
If this is to scale, the distance between the
tractor and the bridge is 100 meters...

00:12:56.141 --> 00:13:02.439
...and we'll assume you can actually string a
piano wire two meters above the ground.

00:13:03.482 --> 00:13:07.402
The distance is 100 meters, with a piano
wire two meters above the surface.

00:13:07.444 --> 00:13:12.908
We'll assume the person hanging on
the wire is about 40 kilograms.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:18.330
In order to-not touch the ground,-the
wire can only descend 1.3 meters.

00:13:18.747 --> 00:13:25.962
Assuming the piano wire has a radius of
live millimeters, the calculated force...

00:13:26.505 --> 00:13:27.839
...would be 500 kilograms.

00:13:29.216 --> 00:13:30.008
<i>That’s right!</i>

00:13:30.425 --> 00:13:32.928
He calculated that in his head?

00:13:33.261 --> 00:13:37.766
Simply put, a tractor of that size
couldn't possibly support that.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:39.184
That's right.

00:13:39.768 --> 00:13:43.230
Saburoumaru‘s theory is impossible.

00:13:43.772 --> 00:13:45.357
N-No way...

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.069
Dan-Sensei, is there any other
information from the scene?

00:13:49.819 --> 00:13:50.695
That's right!

00:13:51.446 --> 00:13:55.408
The perpetrator could have entered the room...

00:13:57.285 --> 00:14:00.372
Was anything found in the student's room?

00:14:00.997 --> 00:14:03.041
Yes, that's good thinking.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.877
Please look at these.

00:14:06.628 --> 00:14:11.800
These are card representations of the
items found in the victim's room.

00:14:14.302 --> 00:14:15.262
A compass.

00:14:16.555 --> 00:14:17.305
A thermos.

00:14:20.016 --> 00:14:20.850
A cell phone.

00:14:22.227 --> 00:14:24.312
A utility knife and a flashlight.

00:14:25.689 --> 00:14:27.023
Some rope and a camera.

00:14:28.275 --> 00:14:30.360
A shovel and life presenter.

00:14:31.278 --> 00:14:35.949
A rubber raft, an air pump and a sleeping bag.

00:14:37.117 --> 00:14:41.037
These were the items found in a large
backpack within the room.

00:14:41.955 --> 00:14:45.667
Ah, the item that could be a clue is...

00:14:49.671 --> 00:14:50.463
That's it!

00:14:50.797 --> 00:14:51.339
Huh?

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:52.591
I've solved it!

00:14:53.174 --> 00:14:54.676
The Case of the Disappearance into Thin Air.

00:15:01.667 --> 00:15:02.418
I've solved it!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.503
The Case of the Disappearance into Thin Air.

00:15:05.588 --> 00:15:06.380
That's not good.

00:15:07.506 --> 00:15:12.511
The footprints begin from the student's room...

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:16.056
...and vanish thirty meters down the field.

00:15:17.224 --> 00:15:21.312
If we assume the perpetrator somehow
began at the middle...

00:15:21.729 --> 00:15:24.356
...and walked backwards
through the fields, then...

00:15:25.566 --> 00:15:27.735
There's only one possible answer.

00:15:28.194 --> 00:15:30.362
Therefore, it's this card!

00:15:41.165 --> 00:15:41.582
Hmm?

00:15:42.666 --> 00:15:43.542
The card...

00:15:47.463 --> 00:15:48.505
There are two hints!

00:15:48.964 --> 00:15:49.757
Huh?

00:15:49.924 --> 00:15:53.636
First, the fact that it was before
the planting season.

00:15:54.637 --> 00:15:56.347
And the second is this...

00:15:57.681 --> 00:15:58.557
The rubber raft!

00:16:00.142 --> 00:16:01.018
The raft?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:05.439
How does someone vanish
from the field using that?

00:16:06.065 --> 00:16:11.445
The perpetrator used this to reach
the middle of the field.

00:16:12.571 --> 00:16:16.533
Of course, you can't use the. boat
when the water is drained.

00:16:17.201 --> 00:16:23.040
The perpetrator must have flooded
the field with the flood gate.

00:16:24.208 --> 00:16:25.918
Isn't that right, Dan-Sensei?

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:27.544
Let's see.

00:16:34.677 --> 00:16:35.719
Wow!

00:16:36.095 --> 00:16:39.056
The gate opened and the field
is flooded with water.

00:16:41.433 --> 00:16:44.770
Eh? This is a well designed diorama.

00:16:45.271 --> 00:16:47.398
Then that means...

00:16:48.732 --> 00:16:51.068
I found it, a miniature rubber raft!

00:16:52.861 --> 00:16:54.822
With plenty of water...

00:16:55.322 --> 00:16:59.743
...the perpetrator set up the raft
and opened the drain gate.

00:17:03.831 --> 00:17:09.169
Then, he quickly paddled the raft to the middle.

00:17:13.841 --> 00:17:16.093
When the water was drained...

00:17:16.593 --> 00:17:19.430
...he stood in the middle with the victim's shoes...

00:17:24.143 --> 00:17:27.604
...and while carrying the raft...

00:17:36.864 --> 00:17:42.036
...he returned to the victim's
room walking backwards.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.622
This is how the victim vanished without a trace!

00:17:52.254 --> 00:17:55.215
The hotel room window was probably
open from the beginning.

00:17:56.258 --> 00:18:01.055
It was opened when the perpetrator
snack in to kidnap the victim...

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:05.392
\
...or to kill him.

00:18:07.936 --> 00:18:08.687
I see.

00:18:09.438 --> 00:18:11.815
Has A Class reached the same solution?

00:18:11.857 --> 00:18:14.818
V-Yes, sir, but hold on!

00:18:15.361 --> 00:18:18.238
We were the first to notice the trick!

00:18:18.947 --> 00:18:19.740
That's right!

00:18:20.115 --> 00:18:22.826
Q Class jumped in and took over!

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.288
We had the right to answer first!

00:18:26.955 --> 00:18:27.873
That's right!

00:18:28.248 --> 00:18:29.416
What are you talking about?

00:18:29.708 --> 00:18:31.543
Kyuu took the card first!

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.129
As they say, "the early bird gets the worm."

00:18:35.005 --> 00:18:36.715
It's not a game of cards!

00:18:37.049 --> 00:18:39.343
N-Now, now, everyone, please calm down.

00:18:40.302 --> 00:18:40.928
Dan-Sensei...

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:43.555
...please make a decision on the winner!

00:18:43.972 --> 00:18:47.476
It's Q Class, right Dan-Sensei?

00:18:47.935 --> 00:18:48.685
Dan-Sensei!

00:18:49.186 --> 00:18:50.687
W-Wait!

00:18:51.355 --> 00:18:53.732
Hmm, this is bad.

00:18:58.695 --> 00:19:01.156
Oh well, unfortunately time's up.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:04.535
Let's call this battle a tie.

00:19:04.743 --> 00:19:06.120
A tie?
A tie?

00:19:08.914 --> 00:19:11.917
I have an important meeting to attend.

00:19:12.751 --> 00:19:20.300
The true battle between Q Class and A Class will
have to wait until the Class Seating Examinations.

00:19:20.843 --> 00:19:22.886
Well then, if you'll excuse me.

00:19:23.679 --> 00:19:25.264
S-Sensei...

00:19:25.764 --> 00:19:26.390
Hmm?

00:19:33.188 --> 00:19:35.315
Well then, if you'll excuse me.

00:19:35.482 --> 00:19:36.984
Thank yaw very much!
Thank you very much!

00:19:42.406 --> 00:19:44.158
Well, that was interesting.

00:19:45.868 --> 00:19:48.537
Both classes are good, but...

00:19:49.163 --> 00:19:52.708
...I couldn't make a reckless decision like that.

00:19:58.255 --> 00:20:00.883
I'm glad the bell rang at the perfect time.

00:20:01.216 --> 00:20:02.968
It's looks like you're enjoying yourself, Nanami.

00:20:03.719 --> 00:20:05.262
T-That voice...

00:20:06.555 --> 00:20:07.848
Dan-Sensei!

00:20:08.265 --> 00:20:12.019
You disguised yourself as me to
amuse yourself, didn't you?

00:20:12.519 --> 00:20:15.230
It was just a childish thing.

00:20:15.606 --> 00:20:17.357
You saw that?

00:20:19.067 --> 00:20:19.651
Well, anyway...

00:20:20.986 --> 00:20:23.489
...I've made my decision.

00:20:24.656 --> 00:20:25.491
Huh?

00:20:29.286 --> 00:20:30.454
I was getting nervous.

00:20:31.163 --> 00:20:33.040
I didn't know what was going to happen.

00:20:33.624 --> 00:20:37.628
We can't lose our Q Class status that easily.

00:20:37.961 --> 00:20:39.296
You were pretty worried.

00:20:39.505 --> 00:20:41.048
So were you, Kinta!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:46.220
Well, we're still top thanks to Kyuu.

00:20:46.803 --> 00:20:49.848
Realizing it was the raft was pretty brilliant.

00:20:51.725 --> 00:20:55.521
T-Then why are you always beating me?

00:20:56.605 --> 00:20:57.147
Huh?

00:20:57.189 --> 00:20:58.315
Dan-sensei!
Dan-sensei!

00:20:59.024 --> 00:21:01.568
Your deduction was quite good.

00:21:02.486 --> 00:21:04.613
I reached the same solution.

00:21:05.656 --> 00:21:08.450
I have the confidence now to send you out.

00:21:09.493 --> 00:21:11.870
What do you mean, Dan-Sensei?

00:21:12.579 --> 00:21:14.957
I want to send you to Kamikakushi village.

00:21:15.666 --> 00:21:17.084
Kamikakushi village?
Kamikakushi village?

00:21:17.626 --> 00:21:20.921
In the neighboring villages of
Kamikakushi and Hyoutan...

00:21:21.713 --> 00:21:25.926
...in the past decade, seven
people have disappeared.

00:21:26.426 --> 00:21:28.220
Seven missing in the past decade?

00:21:29.054 --> 00:21:29.721
Therefore...

00:21:30.055 --> 00:21:36.728
I want all of you to investigate...

00:21:37.437 --> 00:21:43.652
...and discover how, who and why these
disappearances are occurring.

00:21:44.152 --> 00:21:46.446
Eh? So you mean, this case...

00:21:46.822 --> 00:21:49.408
...is still unsolved?

00:21:50.534 --> 00:21:51.201
Dan-Sensci!

00:21:55.414 --> 00:21:57.165
I realize this may be too early...

00:21:57.749 --> 00:21:59.543
...but I have faith in all of you.

00:22:01.128 --> 00:22:06.008
I repeat, I am leaving the resolution
of this case to you.

00:22:06.925 --> 00:22:07.551
Yes, sir!
Yes, sir!

00:22:10.679 --> 00:22:16.518
And so, this is how the Kamikakushi
village case began for Q Class.

00:22:17.227 --> 00:22:18.186
Pants, check!

00:22:18.353 --> 00:22:19.229
Shirts, check!

00:22:19.938 --> 00:22:21.815
And, I have plenty of snacks.

00:22:22.232 --> 00:22:23.358
Everything's perfect.

00:22:24.026 --> 00:22:24.901
Let's see, what am I missing...

00:22:25.402 --> 00:22:26.528
Oh, I almost forgot...

00:22:27.237 --> 00:22:29.197
...I can't leave without this.

00:22:32.409 --> 00:22:34.286
I love this DDS notebook.

00:22:34.953 --> 00:22:37.956
It's so cool that I feel motivated when I hold it!

00:22:38.957 --> 00:22:40.876
Kyuu, are you ready?

00:22:41.168 --> 00:22:42.544
Yeah, almost!

00:22:46.548 --> 00:22:48.383
Kyuu, please take this with you.

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:49.509
Hmm, what is it?

00:22:49.843 --> 00:22:51.678
I got it from the neighborhood shrine.

00:22:52.387 --> 00:22:53.347
It's a talisman.

00:22:57.643 --> 00:22:58.769
Be careful, okay?

00:22:59.519 --> 00:23:02.397
Don't do anything reckless.

00:23:03.231 --> 00:23:04.274
Thank you, mom!

00:23:04.941 --> 00:23:06.109
I know!

00:23:07.194 --> 00:23:10.489
I'll put this at the bottom where it will be safe.

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:14.159
<i>Please protect him, dear.</i>

00:23:15.035 --> 00:23:15.827
<i>Our Kyuu.</i>

00:23:24.211 --> 00:23:26.546
But, what awaited us...

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:32.469
...was a case far more frightening and
complex than we had imagined.

00:23:37.259 --> 00:23:40.466
The Sun is setting in a red glow...

00:23:41.057 --> 00:23:43.598
...as it follows me.

00:23:43.962 --> 00:23:46.763
Along this deserted beach...

00:23:46.759 --> 00:23:50.693
...I walk alone once more.

00:23:50.706 --> 00:23:54.075
I can't continue to hold in...

00:23:54.730 --> 00:23:57.090
...the tears that should pour out.

00:23:57.738 --> 00:24:00.167
Why have these memories...

00:24:00.169 --> 00:24:03.699
...become so wonderful?

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:09.266
Ah... Like an ocean wave, I return to you...

00:24:09.516 --> 00:24:12.039
...because I'm so in love.

00:24:12.772 --> 00:24:15.757
And, now my heart...

00:24:15.757 --> 00:24:17.900
...is heavy with pain.

00:24:18.854 --> 00:24:21.794
Reflections of a bright rainbow...

00:24:21.928 --> 00:24:26.057
...shine on the distant shores of yesterday.

00:24:26.408 --> 00:24:30.028
I'll never forget those days...

00:24:30.035 --> 00:24:35.121
...and I long to see you again.

00:24:37.136 --> 00:24:42.057
The Case of the Kamikakushi Village Disappearances
takes us deep into the mountains...

00:24:42.308 --> 00:24:44.143
...where legendary treasures of
the Japanese army await us.

00:24:44.643 --> 00:24:47.021
We'll expose the dark secrets of this peaceful village!

00:24:47.646 --> 00:24:51.066
After we began our investigation,
there's another disappearance.

00:24:51.650 --> 00:24:53.611
What happened to that lovely reporter?

00:24:54.069 --> 00:24:55.237
There's only one answer!

00:24:56.906 --> 00:24:58.824
Kyuu, please take this with you too.

00:24:58.949 --> 00:24:59.658
They're pickled plums.

00:24:59.783 --> 00:25:00.534
Thank you!

00:25:00.576 --> 00:25:02.620
Also, I bought you new pajamas...

00:25:02.786 --> 00:25:04.997
...a stomach wrap for colds...

00:25:09.043 --> 00:25:09.752
And also...

00:25:10.588 --> 00:25:11.265
Mom...
